Write a function sat_prod that takes two unsigned 32-bit numbers a and b and returns their product as an unsigned 8-bit number, saturated: a product above 255 gives 255. Write and use a helper function sat8(x) that turns an unsigned 32-bit number into an unsigned 8-bit number, giving 255 for anything above 255. Unsigned 32-bit arithmetic wraps around modulo 2^32 (it never traps).
